From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] loader: emulate RDRAND, RDSEED, CLFLUSHOPT, CLZERO, RDPRU and
 RDFSBASE/RDGSBASE on the PS4's CPU

The PS5's Zen 2 has these, the PS4's Jaguar stops on each with an illegal
instruction (checked on the PS4). None of the tested games use them; they are
added so a game that does keeps running. They are rare, so they are emulated
when they trap rather than rewritten at load time:

- RDRAND, RDSEED: a SplitMix64 number from a random seed (getrandom) and a
  counter, CF set and OF/SF/ZF/AF/PF clear. Not for cryptographic keys.
- CLFLUSHOPT: CLFLUSH of the same line, as CLWB already was.
- CLZERO: zeroes the 64-byte line rAX points into.
- RDPRU: MPERF and APERF (ECX 0 and 1) both read the TSC; other registers
  read 0 with CF clear.
- RDFSBASE, RDGSBASE: the thread's base from arch_prctl, what the
  instruction gives on a PC that has it.

XSAVEC and WRFSBASE/WRGSBASE are not emulated.
